Z||000006||Eric||06-13-2001||10:43 PM||||Travis, I need that stuff man.  Okay, if I get the wet kit, how little can I jet it for?  My internals, although stronger than stock, aren't 100% forged, so I want to play it safe (GT is daily driver).  Can you describe the installation process for the Fiero?  I know it only took you a few hours to do, but what the hell do you have to do exactly?  Is there just one injector for the n2o and fuel?  Where does it go, in the manifold, throttle body, before the throttle body?  How difficult is it to splice the fuel line?  Did you use a bigger pump?  Do you still need larger injectors?  Are you using the stock computer?<P>Jonathan, in case you're wondering, that turbo's going in the trash along with the rest of the car.  It is just way too small to screw around with.  Nitrous is the fix I need  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
