Z||000008||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||12:29 AM||||If you want to run NOS the cheapest adj. kit I have found and the most adaptible is the kit for the Mustang F/I 5.0! Thats the kit I use on my Firebird. <BR>Can pick it up for $450 and up.<BR>If you want to use the MSD  multi step retard or other electronics, order stuff for the 93-95 Camaro/Firbird V8. Its the same as the Fiero. I use a F-body wiring harness adapter to run my MSD 6AL on the Fiero. <BR>Lemme know if you need any more info.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000009||1FST2M6||06-14-2001||09:09 AM||||NOS is ok NX is WAY better/Safer/Faster... ok installation is really straight forward... here goes...<P>mount bottle, locate arming switch inside the car, mount the activation switch on the throttle body, run the line from the bottle to the nitrous solenoid, pull the cap off the fuel rail schrader valve and remove the schrader valve.. attach supplied fuel line and run to the fuel solenoid. mount the solenoid out of sight and drill 7/16 hole in intake tube for single nitrous/fuel nozzle and attach the nozzle with the supplied line from the fuel and nitrous solenoid with propper included jets.  wire in the solenoids and go have your bottle filled. (you can't ship a full nitrous bottle) once you are sure that your solenoids BOTH open at WOT and only then, drive the car and listen; tip in to WOT and out a few times to make sure it's really working right .. the solenoids are just a heavy valve and they are loud (sounds like breaking a pencil X2) then turn on the bottle and hit an open road take a fire extinguisher with you just incase you wired somthing wrong.. i've never needed mine. (mine is mounted in the car) get in to 2nd or 3rd at about 2500rpm and arm the system and STAND ON THE THROTTLE!!! if the tires break loose and you feel like your gunna throw up, your nitrous works. if not... e-mail me and i'll give you my 800 help line number and i'll re-walk you through the set-up...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> the NX kit is $450 and has everything you need for all the connections and wiring. on a stock motor you can run a 50shot all day and not worry about it.. on a car with hypereutectic pistons you'll need to run it way richer which will drop the HP rating but still be HELLA fun. my SE was making a weak 170hp on nitrous but a front wheel lifitng 310lbft at the wheels!! (yes Pound Feet LBFT is a measure of torque. sorry i didn't clarify that earlier) I had a MSD 6AL on my SE and just a 6A on the current GT and the install on it took about 45 min and my 15y/o brother inlaw did it while i was at work .. thats how easy it is. my wife hooked up the MSD Digital 6+ on her miata in about an hour and a half with NO help from me.. MSDs are easy to install and make a huge difference if your bottle fed or other forced induction ride. <P><BR>steven - <A HREF="http://cnmmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://cnmmotorsports.com/</A>   the guy used to be at the shop (got my turbos from him actually) and has kinda closed up shop (only does select cars )and is workin on his Dr.s in some kinda real surgery.. James has a Dr.s in Physics... the white car is the president of the San Deigo (sp) starion chapter... CMN burned the chips for my cars. and are you having traction issues with your fiero? I was runnin 13.6@103 and your just breaking 14 at 93. seems like you should have better ETs with those mph numbers... ||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||06-14-2001||09:15 AM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nozzle1.gif">   <P>the top connection is fuel the bottom is nitrous... all the go fast you'll ever need. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>  decent torque for a street car.. a 5 minute jet change and it was a different beast. for those not sure what the relationship Torque and HP have... well instead of another long drawn out explination  Horsepower sells cars, Torque wins races. and telling a kid in a S/C mustang that you just WAXED his @ss with only a 30shot of nitrous is way more pain full then explaining to him that you out torque him by 70+lbft and you weigh less and have better traction due to your weight distribution. <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||11:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>NOS is ok NX is WAY <P>steven - <A HREF="http://cnmmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://cnmmotorsports.com/</A>   the guy used to be at the shop (got my turbos from him actually) and has kinda closed up shop (only does select cars )and is workin on his Dr.s in some kinda real surgery.. James has a Dr.s in Physics... the white car is the president of the San Deigo (sp) starion chapter... CMN burned the chips for my cars. and are you having traction issues with your fiero? I was runnin 13.6@103 and your just breaking 14 at 93. seems like you should have better ETs with those mph numbers... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ah, so you know of James at Custom Network Motors? I hear he had some nice "trick" turbo upgrades. Its a shame he ripped all those people of and closed shop. There is like 50 people on the StarQuest list putting some kinda lawsuit against him. What a shame.<P>Yeah, Fiero has some problems I have been trying to sort out. Never really wanted to beat on her at the track (too much!).<BR>If you want to see a really messed up MPH/VRS ET look at my Firebirds timeslip.<BR>with a 118mph trap speed I "should" be in the 11's. Thanks GM for that stupid rear suspension! 1.9 was my best ever 60ft time. 2.2 is the norm with the bird. Oh....I dont spray her in 1st gear either. Diff couldnt handle much of that w/o breaking.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
