Z||000013||trigger||06-14-2001||04:22 PM||||Eric,<BR>If you don't mind my asking what turbo stuff do you have?  I'm thinking about building a twin turbo 2.5 this summer.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||06:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>HEHE&gt;. he does good work when he's around.. but he stiffed the shop for 3 months rent and split... won't answer e-mails changed his phone numbers and moved! the shop owner has his own suite too... he's name isn't really james it's Bruce -somthing-  you have is aol screen names? i've got em... <P>your diff breaks!?! thought about a detriot locker or a spool? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah the guys on the list have contacted the BBS and AG in GA to file their claim. The GA StarQuest club had nothing but good things to say about CNM when he was "legit". I hate to see things happen like that. <P>Break! HA! Did you know the rear diff in the F-bodys started life in a Vega?! Tiny carrier and axles. I dont know how or what GM was thinking. To put such a weak diff behind an engine that produces over 345ftlbs stock is is crazy!<BR>No way I would think of running a spool on the street. <P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
