Z||000020||kslish||06-16-2001||04:55 PM||||Hehehe.... nitrous on a Duke.<P>5 minutes of fun then BANG!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(visions of broken connecting rods going through the block)<P>Of course, anything is possible if you have enough money to throw at it (better pistons, heavy duty connecting rods...the block and crank would still be question points though, unless they were Super Duty parts).<P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Coupe'N||06-16-2001||05:30 PM||||Thanks for the info kslish. I knew that the bottom end was weak. I didn't know how weak. Is the block REALLY a weak part of the duke? I figured the connecting rods, pistons, and maybe the crank would need to be replaced but didn't think about the block itself. Hmmm.. doesn't really sound like a good bang for the buck in the dukes situation. Having to replace the block, pistons, rods, and crank, then purchase a $500 kit of Nos JUST FOR 50 hp.   <BR>What are you opinions on that matter?? PLEASE don't flame! haha I know how you v6'ers are  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||5
